DFCFD (default domain flow file) is a 72-character string built from up to
45 characters of the installation path followed by the 34 characters of
'/training/CFD_room/zones/room1.dfd'. With an installation path longer than
38 characters the internal WRITE overflows and every program aborts at
start-up with "Fortran runtime error: End of record". Cap the installation
path at 38 characters, as the neighbouring defaults are capped to fit their
strings; the full path is read afterwards from the installation's default
file.

--- a/src/common/startup.F
+++ b/src/common/startup.F
@@ -1430,7 +1430,7 @@
      &    'training/basic/nets/bld_basic_af1.afn'
         write(DPNF,'(2a)') di(1:min(ln,31)),
      &    '/training/plant/vent_simple/cfg/vent.cfg'
-        write(DFCFD,'(2a)') di(1:min(ln,45)),
+        write(DFCFD,'(2a)') di(1:min(ln,38)),
      &    '/training/CFD_room/zones/room1.dfd'
         write(DEFRLB,'(2a)') di(1:min(ln,51)),'/databases/test.res'
         write(DAFRES,'(2a)') di(1:min(ln,51)),'/databases/test.mfr'
